    {
      "type": "instruction",
      "text": "Principle 17. History"
    },
    {
      "type": "sentences",
      "items": [
        {
          "n": "214",
          "text": "Once upon a time the king of heaven, Hwanin sent his son Hwanung"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "to earth."
    },
    {
      "type": "sentences",
      "items": [
        {
          "n": "215",
          "text": "There he married Ungnyo who changed from a bear into a woman."
        },
        {
          "n": "216",
          "text": "She gave birth to a son named Tangun."
        },
        {
          "n": "217",
          "text": "He became the founder of Korea."
        },
        {
          "n": "218",
          "text": "After Gojoson fell, the Korean Peninsula was made into three kingdoms;"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Goguryo, Baekje and Shilla."
    },
    {
      "type": "sentences",
      "items": [
        {
          "n": "219",
          "text": "Later these three kingdoms joined as a single nation called the Shilla."
        },
        {
          "n": "220",
          "text": "It was called the golden age of Korean history."
        },
        {
          "n": "221",
          "text": "The Korean War started in 1950."
        },
        {
          "n": "222",
          "text": "It divided the Korean Peninsula into South and North Korea."
        },
        {
          "n": "223",
          "text": "After the war, our country developed very quickly."
        },
        {
          "n": "224",
          "text": "Since then the country has continued to grow."
        },
        {
          "n": "225",
          "text": "We hosted the Olympic Games and the FIFA World Cup."
        },
        {
          "n": "226",
          "text": "I'm very proud of my country."
        }
      ]
    },
